{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Adjacent to</b> \"You shall not move your neighbor's boundary marker\" — to the murderer: that one should not say, since it is permitted to kill the murderer, I will move his boundary, so that his property not be more stringent than his body." "<b>From Israel and good for you</b> — you shall not move. For on account of moving a boundary the House was destroyed, as it is written: הוי מגיעי בית בבית (Woe to those who add house to house)." "<b>You shall not move a boundary</b> — a warning to the court, that they not exchange any one of the cities of refuge for another city." "<b>To possess it</b> — and adjacent to it: לא יקום עד אחד באיש. That he cannot testify up to here, even your entire boundary, and that is monetary." "<b>For any עון</b> — this is lives." "<b>For any חטאת</b> — this is a sacrifice. Above it is written על פי שנים עדים, and here it speaks of monetary law, and they do not intimidate them as much as in cases of lives."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:05.629629895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}